<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Namibia Q1 pre-capex net drops.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Namibia Q1 pre-capex net drops.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending 15.63 vs 24.41</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  2.99 vs  6.24</p>
<p>    Sales					55.03 vs  6.83</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  248,000 vs  38,000</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates produced (tonnes unless stated):</p>
<p>    - copper				   2,948 vs    768</p>
<p>    - lead					 917 vs    114</p>
<p>    - silver (kg)				  8 vs	9</p>
<p>Metal produced fromsmeleters (tonnes unless stated):</p>
<p>    - copper				   4,557 vs     78</p>
<p>    - lead					 120 vs  1,340</p>
<p>    - silver (kg)				 10 vs    -</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields of Namibia Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - Production was hit in the preceding quarter by a strike and in the first quarter of 1997 by flooding and smelter commissionng problems</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
